::scene COLD_OPEN

EVENT FADE_IN

SHOT
Cut to Neil's basement. 

The screen holds black. In the deep background, footsteps approach slowly through darkness. A faint reverb hangs in the air — the acoustic signature of a basement. Above it, muffled but unmistakable, the din of a bustling Vietnamese laundromat drifts down through the ceiling.
SHOT_END

Neil Mcmanistan:
FUCK!

ACTION npc_neil_mcmanistan trips violently over a chair, which screeches across the concrete floor and detonates into a wall of empty beer cans and food containers.

SHOT
A bare lightbulb swings into frame on its pull-string. It flickers on, casting a slow pendulum of amber light across a dishevelled man in a dirty wife-beater seated at a table. In front of him sits a microphone from the 1930s.
SHOT_END

CAM 1 PULL_BACK on Neil McManistan at the table

SHOT
The camera slowly pulls back. The host is wearing combat boots. He is not wearing pants. These two facts are presented without comment.
SHOT_END

Neil Mcmanistan:
you're not gonna believe this shit!

CAM 2 SIDE_PROFILE on Neil McManistan

ACTION npc_neil_mcmanistan pulls out a Zippo lighter and ignites a cigarette with the ease of a man who has been doing this since before it was legal.

TITLE divorced	

EVENT DISSOLVE

SHOT
The basement dissolves to a sprawling conspiracy web: cork board, yarn, thumbtacks. Charlie Kirk is connected to Benito Mussolini by a red string. Both are connected to a laminated photograph of a lizard. Scattered across the map: celebrities, geopolitical figures, and anti-Zionist imagery of considerable ambition. It is the work of a very troubled and extremely productive man.
SHOT_END

SHOT
The scene snaps into a hard spin cut — synchronized to the wet, gurgling crescendo of a bong reaching its full percolation. We slam back to the basement.
SHOT_END

ACTION npc_neil_mcmanistan doubles over the table in a monumental coughing fit, a thick cloud of smoke escaping in every direction.

CAM 1 CLOSEUP on Neil McManistan

::scene ACT_1

Neil Mcmanistan:
They must think that I'm retarded. You'd have to be retarded not to put this together, and as sure as Barb took the kids the Jews will get me for this.

Captain Nguyen:
Jesus christ Neil we talked about this shit man you're gonna get us kicked off public access we need this man.

Neil Mcmanistan:
Im sorry, I'm sorry where was I. I'll tell you where I was, I was at the grocery store and they had a coupon, Tim Horton's iced coffee syrup, save 2 dollars. And you know how I feel about Singh Hortons...

Captain Nguyen:
CUT!

SHOT
A beep sounds. Neil nods at the camera. The show resumes.
SHOT_END

ACTION npc_neil_mcmanistan gives the camera a slow, deliberate nod.

CAM 1 CLOSEUP on Neil McManistan

Neil Mcmanistan:
these fuckin grocery barons are sucking us dry! I had this coupon, and lo and behold, ill give it a go, why not save a few bucks. Regular price 8 bucks, brought it down to 6 with the coupon, but i price matched it down to 6 so the coupon made it 4....

Captain Nguyen:
What the fuck are you talking about and get to the point!

SHOT
The Captain Nguyen delivers this in a frantic whisper from somewhere just off-camera. It is not a quiet whisper.
SHOT_END

Neil Mcmanistan:
Anyways I went back into the place for some vittles a week later, no 2 dollar off coupons, but the same bottle of syrup was now 2 dollars cheaper now that there were no coupons. Those greedy pricks they must think that we are SAPS!

ACTION npc_neil_mcmanistan slams his fist on the table. The ashtray goes airborne. The camera jerks up and snaps directly into Neil's face.

CAM 1 SNAP_TIGHT on Neil McManistan

Neil Mcmanistan:
Don't even get me started on that shithole hortons, its harder than Chinese calculus trying to get a jesus coffee in there, they gotta get some teenage girls in there, not like that, not at all, never...

Captain Nguyen:
Jesus christ man you can't keep saying that shit.

Neil Mcmanistan:
Pause, no diddy, respectfully.

Captain Nguyen:
THATS NOT HELPING!

Neil Mcmanistan:
And now a word from our sponsor:

CAM 3 SWING to the far corner of the basement

SHOT
The camera drifts wide to catch the far corner of the basement. Perched on a barstool, just at the edge of the visible set, is an old Vietnamese man. He is holding a small brown paper bag. He has been there the entire time.
SHOT_END

Captain Nguyen:
Who the hell is that?!

Neil Mcmanistan:
Thats fuckin, nguyen, man, hey nguyen say hi.

NGUYEN:
[Extended Vietnamese at considerable volume, followed by a long and deliberate nod.]

Neil Mcmanistan:
Im gonna be this guys sponsor im bringing him on the crew we can hire him for half wage do you believe this guy is from fuckin 'Nam hey nguyen tell this guy you're from 'nam!

ACTION npc_neil_mcmanistan lunges forward and grabs Camera 1, physically wrenching it toward Nguyen.

ACTION npc_captain_nguyen reaches into frame and yanks Camera 1 back in the other direction.

CAM 1 SNAPS_BACK to Neil McManistan

Captain Nguyen:
NEIL WE HAVE TO THANK THE SPONSORS SAY AND NOW A WORD FROM OUR SPONSORS!

SHOT
The Captain Nguyen shouts this at a volume that could be heard in the laundromat upstairs.
SHOT_END

Neil Mcmanistan:
And now a word from our sponsors.

EVENT COMMERCIAL_BREAK

::scene AD_1

TITLE hungry_man_just_meats_logo

SHOT
The basement drops away. We cut to a commercial. A sad man sits alone at a kitchen table, staring at a wall.
SHOT_END

CAM 4 CLOSEUP on the sad man

EVENT DISSOLVE

CAM 5 WIDE dream sequence — sunlit park

SHOT
A dream blooms into colour. The man pushes his child on a playground swing. Nearby, his partner holds a new baby and smiles at him — warm, full, genuine. This is everything. This is his whole life.
SHOT_END

SHOT
A thundercrack. A man on a Harley-Davidson roars up onto the grass, dismounts, kicks the baby, and begins making out with the man's wife. The kid on the swing jumps off, turns to face the camera, and speaks.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
Loser.

SHOT
The whole family piles onto the Harley and rides away without a backward glance. The man sinks to his knees. He begins to weep.
SHOT_END

SHOT
A figure approaches from the right: a large man in a foam rubber Salisbury steak costume. He sits beside the crying man and places an arm around him in silence.

A second figure approaches from the left: a rectangular man in a chicken patty costume, carrying a glass of whiskey. He hands it over.

A third figure lumbers in from the rear — shaped like a rib patty, boombox on one shoulder. Creed is playing. He reaches a thick slab-like arm forward and passes the crying man a lit joint.
SHOT_END

EVENT DISSOLVE

SHOT
The man is back in his kitchen. He is cleaned up. Shaved. Wearing a pressed shirt. On the table before him sits a Hungry Man dinner tray — wall to wall meat. Not a vegetable in sight. He looks at it the way a man looks at his oldest friend.
SHOT_END

NARRATOR:
It's just the meats.

NARRATOR:
She can't control you anymore, king.

EVENT RETURN_FROM_BREAK

SHOT
The camera fades back to the basement. Neil is at the table. There are three more cigarette butts in the ashtray than there were before the break. He does not acknowledge this. The pendulum bulb has slowed to a gentle sway.
SHOT_END

CAM 1 MEDIUM on Neil McManistan

::scene ACT_2

Neil Mcmanistan:
Where was I...

Captain Nguyen:
Maybe we should move on.

Neil Mcmanistan:
MAYBE YOU SHOULD MOVE ON!

Captain Nguyen:
You know that's not what I meant. Let's get to the top 10.

Neil Mcmanistan:
OK here's my top ten conspiracy theories of the week, as always I will be fielding calls but only at the end of the programme please, I know our phone lines are already lighting up, our operators are standing by...

Captain Nguyen:
No one calls this show. This phone isn't even that type of phone. It's a payphone. You have a basement payphone. I didn't even think that was possible.

Neil Mcmanistan:
She fuckin took everything man...

Captain Nguyen:
Let's try and move on.

Neil Mcmanistan:
That's what Barb told my kids and my dog.

Captain Nguyen:
For christ sake.

Neil Mcmanistan:
Just put the fuckin number up man, put up my number so my fans can call in.

TICKER
1-800-273-8255 ←── NEIL'S HOTLINE — OPERATORS STANDING BY ←── 1-800-273-8255 ←── CENTAUR SHREDS ON ←── DON'T LET HER WIN, BROTHER! — HULK HOGAN ←── CALL NOW ←── 1-800-273-8255 ←── NEIL'S HOTLINE ←──
TICKER_END

SHOT
The number crawls across the bottom of the screen. It is the suicide hotline. It is being towed by a centaur playing electric guitar. Behind the centaur, a graphic element features Hulk Hogan pointing directly at the audience with one finger. He appears to be saying something encouraging.
SHOT_END

Neil Mcmanistan:
WHAT THE FUCK WAS THAT MAN?! WAS THAT THE SUICIDE HOTLINE NUMBER?!

Neil Mcmanistan:
And why was Hulk Hogan involved?

Captain Nguyen:
The Hulkster was your idea.

Neil Mcmanistan:
Why the hell was it my idea when was that ever my idea to have Hulk Hogan telling my audience not to kill themselves?!

Captain Nguyen:
I got a voicemail at 3 am. It sounded like you were drunk but you were quite insistent that we should use the Hulkster in a graphic for the show.

Neil Mcmanistan:
Since when did that mean get the Hulkster to tell my fans not to kill themselves after the divorce?! I was watching the Netflix documentary!

Captain Nguyen:
That's on me. I thought you'd appreciate the levity.

Neil Mcmanistan:
The Hulkster wouldn't stand for this. It was all a smear anyways, and we all know why...

Captain Nguyen:
What are you talking about man?

Neil Mcmanistan:
These Hollywood jews hate to see a blonde haired blue eyed macho friend of Jesus win.

Captain Nguyen:
You can't keep saying jews!

Neil Mcmanistan:
Why is Barb gonna go get her big jew lawyer to come after me, you know they love to litigate —

Captain Nguyen:
Jesus!

Neil Mcmanistan:
YOU CANT SQUEEZE BLOOD FROM A STONE BARBRA I KNOW WHO DROVE US APART AND I HEARS THE TRUTH IS REALLY BAD!

Neil Mcmanistan:
IS REALLY BAD.

Neil Mcmanistan:
ISRAELI BAD!

Neil Mcmanistan:
PRESS THE RED BUTTON NGUYEN!

CAM 3 SWING to Nguyen in the corner

ACTION npc_nguyen reaches out and presses the large red button mounted to the wall beside his barstool.

SHOT
From a speaker of indeterminate location, a single word is announced at considerable volume.
SHOT_END

CAM 1 BACK to Neil McManistan

Captain Nguyen:
You can't have a Jew button are you insane!

Neil Mcmanistan:
THEN WHY DO THESE JEWS KEEP PUSHING MY BUTTONS?!

Captain Nguyen:
I'm cutting to break.

ACTION npc_neil_mcmanistan seizes Camera 1 and wrenches it toward Nguyen.

ACTION npc_captain_nguyen grabs Camera 1 from the other side and hauls it back.

SHOT
The camera swings wildly between the two men, catching ceiling, floor, the laundromat pipes, and half-illuminated faces in roughly equal measure.
SHOT_END

Neil Mcmanistan:
DO YOU HAVE TROUBLE GETTING IT UP CUZ YOUR WIFE WAS AN UGLY PIG?!

Captain Nguyen:
Give me that!

Neil Mcmanistan:
WELL LOOK NO FURTHER THAN Captain Nguyen'S MAGIC ROOT! AVAILABLE VIA PAYPAL —

CAM 1 SNAPS to Nguyen's midsection

ACTION npc_nguyen reaches into his trousers and produces a strange, gnarled red root, which he holds aloft with quiet dignity.

Captain Nguyen:
THAT'S ENOUGH! I'VE HAD ENOUGH! I'M PULLING THE PLUG —

Neil Mcmanistan:
She took everything. I'm living off tinned beans here. Let a man eat.

Captain Nguyen:
And now a word from our sponsor.

ACTION npc_captain_nguyen releases Camera 1 and it drops to the concrete floor.

SHOT
The camera hits the floor and settles at a forty-five-degree angle. The image holds there. In the background, the argument continues to dissolve into ambient noise.
SHOT_END

EVENT COMMERCIAL_BREAK

::scene AD_2

TITLE jerry_rosenberg_logo

SHOT
Cut to exterior. California. The sun is aggressively bright. A convertible sports car rolls up a coastal road to the sound of smooth jazz.
SHOT_END

CAM 6 WIDE on the beach

SHOT
The camera pans to the beach. An attractive woman and her handsome personal trainer are doing Pilates together. They are very in sync. They are having a genuinely lovely time.
SHOT_END

SHOT
A man in a crisp linen suit steps into frame. He has the easy confidence of someone who has never once paid his own parking tickets.
SHOT_END

LAWYER:
Do you ever wonder what your life could be, if this guy wasn't holding you back?

SHOT

The footage cuts abruptly to grainy home video: a man in a wife-beater and dirty underpants, cracking a beer and lighting a cigarette while a baby plays with a fork near a wall socket.

SHOT_END

Neil Mcmanistan:
WTF IS THAT ME?!

SHOT
The ad continues, undeterred.
SHOT_END

SHOT
The lawyer steps back into frame. He is now dressed as a mohel. He adjusts his equipment.
SHOT_END

LAWYER:
Let's bris this schmuck. Now cheaper — with our ten percent off circumcision discount! Spouses of gentiles now save ten percent!

Neil Mcmanistan:
YOU LET THEM RUN AN AD FOR MY EX WIFE'S JEW LAWYER?!

Captain Nguyen:
He pays good money —

Neil Mcmanistan:
THAT'S MY MONEY!

Captain Nguyen:
He's a friend of the show.

Neil Mcmanistan:
HE IS NOT A FRIEND OF THE SHOW THIS GUY RUINED MY LIFE —

Captain Nguyen:
I'm muting your microphone.

SHOT
Neil's protests continue at length, reduced by the muted mic to a distant, indistinct hum. The ad presses on without him.
SHOT_END

SHOT
The lawyer returns, now dressed as a Hasid. He squares up to the camera with evident satisfaction. He begins to recite his contact information at a measured pace. Then his eyes go wide. His hands come together — slowly, fingers interlacing.
SHOT_END

LAWYER:
For all your divorce needs, come to Jerry Rosenberg Family Law — where we will make him pay. And make him pay for me too!

SHOT
From somewhere behind the muted microphone, Neil can be observed commenting at some volume. The exact words are inaudible. The feeling is clear.
SHOT_END

EVENT RETURN_FROM_BREAK

SHOT
The camera — which has been lying on the floor of the basement at a forty-five-degree angle for the duration of the break — is picked up by an unseen hand and levelled. It finds Neil already mid-sentence, microphone apparently reinstated.
SHOT_END

CAM 1 MEDIUM on Neil McManistan
Neil Mcmanistan:
Who makes an ad like that? That's like three antisemitic self-burns in a row. He looks like Jude Süss up there. This is egregious! I'm too riled up to continue. Nguyen, roll the credits!

ACTION npc_nguyen rises from his barstool and produces a large flip chart from behind him with the calm efficiency of a man who was prepared for this.

